Needs to return both orphanPrs and push into issueNumbers — pass a `seen` object and return issueNumbers too. Let me make it return { issueNumbers, orphanPrs } with seen as input. CC of the callback: 1 + if(1) + && (1) + if(1) + &&(1) + catch(1) = 6. OK.

Then:

```js
function processIssue(...) // issue loop body
function processOrphan(...) // orphan loop body
``

Actually the loops are:
```js
issueNumbers.forEach(function (n) {
   say('::issue #' + n);
   try {
       var pr = findLinkedPr(openPrs, n, ghBranchPattern);
       if (!pr) { say(...); skipped++; return; }
       var prn = parseInt(pr.number, 10);
       var outcome = runStateMachine(ctx, prn, function (mergedPr) { ...issue post-merge... });
       if (outcome === 'merged') merged++; else skipped++;
