``
`say` is a closure over log — currently defined inside action: `function say(line) { log.push(line); console.log(line); }` and ctx = { owner, name, log }. I'll put `say` into ctx: `ctx.say = say`. runStateMachine uses ctx.log.push — I can extend ctx with a `say` and pass around. Keep runStateMachine unchanged in behavior except the state-decision extraction.

Orphan loop body:
```js
function processOrphanPr(ctx, prn, opts, tally) {
   ctx.say('::PR #' + prn + ' (no linked open issue)');
   try {
