if (typeof v === 'string') return v;
if (v && typeof v.value === 'string') return v.value;
``
→ returns '' string as-is (typeof '' string → return ''), continuing only for non-strings without .value. My scanTransformedFailedReason: `found !== '' || typeof fields[key] === 'string'` — same convoluted pattern. Honestly, simpler and truer to the original:

